From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:47:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] python: Rust host toolchain, cryptography 43.0.3 and
 Reticulum 1.5.2

Reticulum needs PyCA cryptography, which needs Rust. Enable a source-built
Rust host toolchain for riscv64gc-unknown-linux-musl (Tier-3 upstream, no
prebuilt std) via a rustc Config.in.host clause, bump python-cryptography to
43.0.3 with the maturin backend and a per-package host-rust force-overwrite
hook to resolve the rustc/rustlib mismatch, and add a libffi host-build fix.
Add the python-rns recipe (Reticulum 1.5.2).
---
